>reality. Occasionaly, all of us probably notice but shrug it off.

Most people can easily see the flicker if you follow a slow moving object
slowly away from the flickering image and watch the image out of the corner
of your eye. Most theatre projectors have a 80% or better duty cycle (the
time a frame is projected as a percent of the total) so the "off " time
between frames is only 1/160th of a second. 

On a similar theme I'm trying (without much luck) to get the VRML (virtual
reality markup language) specification to include pointers for perceptions
such as rocking, vibration, temperature, humidity, radiant heat, smell,
taste etc. 

I'd like to see pointers to such senses as the feeling someone is watching.
I'm sure there are many more "senses" I can't think of.

 








