	* changes in the local lists host site *

This is just advance notice -- you will recieve further notices when
the host site change is about to happen, and the old addresses will be
aliased to the new addresses.

Since we started having local lists, they have been running on
the machines at the Free Software Foundation (FSF).

Sometime in the next month, hopefully within 2 weeks we (rjc & me),
will be moving those lists to a new host site. That site will be
Powermail.com. There are several reasons we will be doing this:

1) better management of the lists - we have code to do remote admin
   of the gnu lists but it will not run there! I will be able to remotely
   admin these lists giving the same quality of admin as I now provided to
   the main list. (most requests are filled in 4 hours).

2) better software - we will be using MailWeir at PowerMail, which means
   that as we develop MailWeir we will be adding lots of new functionality
   to the local lists. The initial code we will use has majordomo like
   functionality -- we will add lots of radical features through out
   the fall and winter.

	* There is one major disadvantage! *

List turn around. We only exchange e-mail every couple of hours, so
list "speed" will slow down for the near term! 

Your comments and questions are welcome.

